## 15. Authentication, Security and Privacy

Implement:

- Secure authentication.
- Role-based authorization.
- Object-level access control.
- Server-side input validation.
- Rate limiting.
- Secure session handling.
- CSRF protection where applicable.
- Secure CORS configuration.
- Content security policy.
- Upload validation.
- Private file storage.
- Signed URLs for sensitive files.
- Password reset or supported identity recovery.
- Audit logging.
- Secrets management.
- Database least-privilege access.
- Production error monitoring.
- Backup and recovery procedures.

Never trust a client-supplied user ID, supplier ID, commission amount, payment state, or role.

Ensure suppliers can access only their own business records, salespeople can access only authorized orders and earnings, and buyers can access only the specific order granted by their secure token.

Encrypt sensitive account information at rest where appropriate. Mask bank account details in the UI. Never store online banking credentials, bank passwords, or payment PINs.

Minimize collection of identity documents and other sensitive information. Establish retention periods for buyer information, receipts, and verification records.

Have local legal and payment specialists review the proposed operating model, privacy obligations, business contracts, and any payment or stored-value functionality before launch.

